@startuml
title qtooth-ble - shell-triggered encrypted message
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam participantBorderColor #64748B
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #E7F0FA
skinparam noteBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
hide footbox
actor "Shell user" as user
participant "Pi: qtooth-ble\nRust / BlueR / OpenSSL" as pi
participant "Pixel app\nKotlin BLE + Rust core" as phone
user -> pi : send plaintext
pi -> phone : Advertise custom service
phone -> pi : Connect / discover / subscribe
note over pi, phone
Unique provisioned pairing PSK; fresh nonces.
Writes with response toward Pi; indications toward phone.
end note
pi -> pi : Generate ephemeral ML-KEM-768 key pair
loop Bounded application fragments
  pi -> phone : KEM public-key chunks
end
phone -> phone : Encapsulate shared secret
loop Bounded application fragments
  phone -> pi : KEM ciphertext chunks
end
pi -> pi : Decapsulate shared secret
pi <-> phone : Authenticate bound transcript / confirm derived keys
note over pi, phone
HKDF produces session keys/nonce material.
Abort on authentication or reassembly failure.
end note
pi -> phone : AEAD ciphertext + authenticated metadata
phone -> phone : Check sequence/tag; display plaintext
phone -> pi : Authenticated receipt
pi -> user : Result / MTU / fragments / timings
@enduml
